INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt") VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'gates-foundation-ai-fellowship-africa-20261105', 'global', 'Kenya',
'Gates Foundation AI Fellowship 2027: Paid AI Roles in Africa, Apply by 11 November',
'',
'The Gates Foundation is recruiting AI Fellows for its first Africa-based cohort, a 12-month paid role in Nairobi, Abuja, Addis Ababa or Johannesburg, with applications closing on 11 November 2026.',
'',
$$<p>The Gates Foundation AI Fellowship is open for applications for its first Africa-based cohort, a 12-month paid role that puts artificial intelligence to work on health, development and education challenges across the continent. The Gates Foundation is recruiting AI Fellows to be based in Nairobi, Abuja, Addis Ababa or Johannesburg, and applications close on 11 November 2026. The vacancy carries requisition number B021830, and fellows will be employed full time on a limited-term contract rather than enrolled on a study programme.</p>
<p>Read the limits first. Applicants must already be legally authorised to work in the country where the role is based, and the Foundation said it will not provide visa sponsorship or relocation support. That condition rules out anyone who would need a work permit in Nigeria, Kenya, Ethiopia or South Africa, including applicants based in Nepal without existing work authorisation in one of those countries. The posting does not state a salary figure, describing the pay only as competitive under the Foundation's compensation structure, so no salary number can be quoted for this role.</p>
<table><tr><th>At a glance</th><th>Details</th></tr><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>Gates Foundation (Bill &amp; Melinda Gates Foundation), Africa team</td></tr><tr><td>Programme</td><td>AI Fellows Programme 2027, first Africa-based cohort</td></tr><tr><td>Role</td><td>AI Fellow, Africa Regional Offices</td></tr><tr><td>Requisition</td><td>B021830</td></tr><tr><td>Duration</td><td>12 months, full-time, limited-term employment</td></tr><tr><td>Locations</td><td>Nairobi, Kenya; Abuja, Nigeria; Addis Ababa, Ethiopia; or Johannesburg, South Africa</td></tr><tr><td>Application deadline</td><td>11 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>Not stated in the posting; salaried, with Foundation employee benefits</td></tr><tr><td>Work authorisation</td><td>Must already hold the legal right to work in the country of placement; no visa sponsorship or relocation support</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through the Gates Foundation careers portal (Workday)</td></tr></table>
<h2>Gates Foundation AI Fellowship: what fellows will work on</h2>
<p>Fellows join the Foundation's Africa team and work alongside government counterparts and development partners on high-priority projects, with each fellow typically assigned one or two major projects and the chance to contribute to more as priorities change. The Foundation said the work covers health financing and decision support, healthcare supply chains and medicine availability, predictive analytics for healthcare, and AI for global development. Its example projects include decision-support tools that bring health financing data together across countries to find bottlenecks, a prototype to reduce stock-outs of essential medicines at district and facility level, and an AI tool that ranks health interventions against budgets, tracks them through procurement and forecasts stock-out risk.</p>
<p>Day to day, fellows scope AI applications from real operational needs, build prototypes with large language models and modern AI tools, design, develop and evaluate machine learning models, prepare and manage datasets and data pipelines, and build decision-support systems that fit into existing workflows. The Foundation said fellows also run model validation and performance testing, check that AI is used responsibly with attention to fairness, privacy and transparency, and run AI literacy workshops and mentor colleagues in responsible AI use. Fellows are expected to explain technical findings to technical and non-technical audiences alike.</p>
<h2>Who can apply for the Gates Foundation AI Fellowship</h2>
<p>The Foundation said applicants need a bachelor's or master's degree in computer science, data science, engineering, applied mathematics or a related field, plus at least two years of experience applying AI solutions, preferably in healthcare, agriculture, development or related systems. Applicants need a strong grounding in AI and machine learning modelling and evaluation, hands-on experience with large language models including prompting, retrieval, tool use, deployment or adaptation, and software development and data engineering skills strong enough to build end-to-end solutions.</p>
<p>Direct AI research experience is not required, and the Foundation said evidence of ability can come from applied coursework, research, internships or early professional experience. Applicants also need strong written and verbal communication, the ability to work with interdisciplinary teams and adapt as requirements change, and a genuine interest in using AI responsibly to advance public health, education and equitable development. The posting describes the role as suited to AI developers, machine learning engineers, data scientists and technology professionals who want their work to serve social impact.</p>
<h2>What the fellowship pays and what fellows receive</h2>
<p>The fellowship is a salaried 12-month position, and the Foundation said fellows receive its employee benefits, which it describes as comprehensive medical, dental and vision cover with no employee premiums, generous paid time off, paid family leave and Foundation-funded retirement contributions. Fellows also get professional mentorship and exposure to senior leadership and experts across AI, global health, development and policy, plus an international professional network spanning leading non-governmental organisations, governments, academic institutions and development partners.</p>
<p>The Africa cohort follows the Foundation's AI Fellows programmes in the United States and India, and fellows work across its Global Health, Gender Equality, Global Development and Global Growth and Opportunity teams. Because the role is structured as full-time employment, fellows are paid staff for the year rather than grant holders, and the Foundation said the experience is meant to build practical skill in developing, testing and deploying AI solutions for real-world challenges.</p>
<h2>How to apply for the Gates Foundation AI Fellowship</h2>
<p>Start on the Gates Foundation careers site and search for AI Fellow, Africa Regional Offices, using requisition number B021830 to find the vacancy. Read the full role description first, then choose the location where you already hold the legal right to work, since the posting cannot be moved between countries. Prepare a curriculum vitae that shows the AI systems you have built, how you evaluated them and who used them, and submit the application through the Foundation's Workday recruitment portal before 11 November 2026.</p>
<p>Apply only through the official careers portal. The Foundation charges no fee to apply, so anyone asking for payment to secure a place on the fellowship is not acting for the Foundation. With six days left from 5 November 2026, applicants should not leave the application to the final day, and anyone without work authorisation in Nigeria, Kenya, Ethiopia or South Africa should not spend time on a role they cannot take up. Readers tracking other paid AI opportunities may want <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/anthropic-residency-ai-safety-20261104">the Anthropic Residency in AI safety</a>, which closes on 22 November 2026, <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/ai-training-jobs-software-engineers-20261104">AI training jobs for software engineers</a>, and <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/co-operative-bank-kenya-ai-jobs-11-posts-20261105">Co-operative Bank Kenya AI jobs</a>, where most AI and data roles close on 9 November 2026.</p>
<p><small>Sources: OYA Opportunities at https://oyaop.com/opportunity/scholarships-and-fellowships/gates-foundation-ai-fellow-program-2027-paid-ai-fellowship-in-africa-regional-offices/, Opportunities for Youth at https://opportunitiesforyouth.org/2026/11/03/gates-foundation-ai-fellowship-2026-apply-for-a-12-month-ai-fellow-position-in-africa-deadline-november-11/, Opportunity Lab at https://opportunitylab.net/gates-foundation-ai-fellows-africa-2026/ and Ethio NGO Jobs at https://www.ethiongojobs.com/ai-fellow-africa-regional-offices-position-at-the-gates-foundation/, all reporting the official Gates Foundation posting, requisition B021830. The posting states the locations, deadline, eligibility and application route quoted here; the salary is not stated in the posting.</small></p>$$,
'',
ARRAY['https://oyaop.com/opportunity/scholarships-and-fellowships/gates-foundation-ai-fellow-program-2027-paid-ai-fellowship-in-africa-regional-offices/','https://opportunitiesforyouth.org/2026/11/03/gates-foundation-ai-fellowship-2026-apply-for-a-12-month-ai-fellow-position-in-africa-deadline-november-11/','https://opportunitylab.net/gates-foundation-ai-fellows-africa-2026/','https://www.ethiongojobs.com/ai-fellow-africa-regional-offices-position-at-the-gates-foundation/'],
NOW(), NOW(), NOW())
ON CONFLICT ("slug") DO NOTHING;


INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt") VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'va-veterans-service-representative-jobs-20261105', 'global', 'USA',
'VA Veterans Service Representative Jobs: 2,000+ Openings, Pay $50,460–$82,007, First Cutoff 9 November',
'',
'The Department of Veterans Affairs is hiring more than 2,000 Veterans Service Representatives across 60 cities, with the first application cutoff on 9 November 2026.',
'',
$$<p>VA Veterans Service Representative jobs are open across the United States, with the Department of Veterans Affairs hiring more than 2,000 claims processors in fiscal year 2027 to deal with a record workload. The VA said it processed a record 3.1 million claims in the 2026 fiscal year, and the new Veterans Service Representatives will review claims, gather evidence and make decisions on veterans' benefits. The roles are advertised on USAJOBS under Direct Hire Authority, and the first application cutoff is 9 November 2026, so applicants who want to be in the first review group need to move quickly.</p>
<p>Read the limits first. These roles are open to all United States citizens, not only veterans, but applicants must be United States citizens, and the positions are not remote: the work is done on site at VA regional offices, with telework limited to situational approval. The announcement runs as a standing register, which means applications are reviewed in cutoff batches rather than all at once, and anyone who applies after the first cutoff on 9 November 2026 goes into a later batch. The second cutoff is 30 November 2026, and the announcement closes on 21 December 2026.</p>
<table><tr><th>At a glance</th><th>Details</th></tr><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>Department of Veterans Affairs, Veterans Benefits Administration</td></tr><tr><td>Role</td><td>Veterans Service Representative (VSR), series GS-0996</td></tr><tr><td>Vacancies</td><td>More than 2,000 claims processors planned for fiscal year 2027</td></tr><tr><td>Grades</td><td>GS-07, GS-09 and GS-10 career ladder</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>$50,460 to $82,007 a year, depending on location and grade</td></tr><tr><td>Locations</td><td>60 cities nationwide, including Anchorage, Phoenix, Los Angeles, San Diego, Denver, Atlanta, Chicago, Boston, New York, Houston, San Antonio, Seattle, Honolulu and San Juan</td></tr><tr><td>Work mode</td><td>On site; not a remote position</td></tr><tr><td>First cutoff</td><td>9 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Second cutoff</td><td>30 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Closing date</td><td>21 December 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through USAJOBS</td></tr></table>
<h2>VA Veterans Service Representative jobs: what the role involves</h2>
<p>A Veterans Service Representative explains benefit programmes and entitlement criteria to veterans and their families, analyses claims material, identifies the issues in a claim, gathers relevant evidence, conducts interviews, adjudicates claims and inputs the data needed to generate the award and notification letter that tells the veteran the decision and the reason for it. The work is desk-based and decision-heavy: representatives apply laws, regulations and official guidance to judge whether the evidence supports eligibility, and they serve as the primary contact for the veteran or the veteran's representative through the process.</p>
<p>The hiring is driven by volume. The VA said it processed a record 3.1 million claims in the 2026 fiscal year, and the department is bringing in the new representatives to handle that caseload across its regional offices. Because the announcement is a standing register, it establishes an applicant pool that the VA draws on as vacancies arise, rather than filling a fixed number of posts on a single date. The grade progression runs from GS-07 to GS-10, and the announcement said the career ladder allows promotion to the full performance level of GS-10 without further competition once time-in-grade, qualification and performance requirements are met.</p>
<h2>Who can apply for the VA Veterans Service Representative roles</h2>
<p>The announcement is open to all United States citizens. For the GS-07 grade, applicants need at least one year of specialised experience equivalent to the GS-05 level in a federal, state or private setting, or one year of graduate education, or superior academic achievement at bachelor's level. Higher grades need correspondingly more experience, and applicants must meet all requirements by the closing date of the announcement. The work calls for experience in interpreting regulations and applying laws to explain, evaluate and recommend determinations on eligibility for claimant requests.</p>
<p>Applicants must be United States citizens, and the announcement said a background and suitability investigation applies, with Selective Service registration required for males born after 31 December 1959. At the GS-10 level, representatives must complete the VSR Skills Certification. Meeting the minimum eligibility does not guarantee selection, because applications are ranked against the cutoff registers and the VA reviews them in batches as vacancies arise.</p>
<h2>Pay and the career ladder for Veterans Service Representatives</h2>
<p>The advertised pay band of $50,460 to $82,007 a year reflects 2026 locality-adjusted pay, with the exact figure depending on the grade and the city. The GS-07, GS-09 and GS-10 ladder means a representative can advance a grade roughly every 12 months without competing again, provided the requirements are met, and the full performance level is GS-10. The announcement said the position is a full-time permanent role, working Monday to Friday, and the Veterans Benefits Administration fills the posts through Direct Hire Authority, which lets the VA hire faster than the standard competitive process.</p>
<p>The breadth of the hiring is unusual for a single federal occupation: more than 2,000 posts across 60 cities, from Anchorage to San Juan, makes this one of the broadest VA civilian hiring pushes of the year. The posts sit in Veterans Service Centres at regional offices, so applicants should choose a location they can actually work from, since the role cannot be done remotely.</p>
<h2>How to apply for VA Veterans Service Representative jobs</h2>
<p>Go to USAJOBS and search for Veterans Service Representative, series GS-0996, then choose the nationwide standing-register announcement and the location that suits you. Prepare a federal-style resume and the documents the announcement asks for, and submit before 9 November 2026 to be considered in the first cutoff. Applications are reviewed in cutoff batches, with later reviews roughly every three weeks until the announcement closes on 21 December 2026, so a late application still counts but waits for a later batch.</p>
<p>Apply only through USAJOBS. The VA charges no fee to apply, and no agent or third party can move an application forward, so anyone asking for payment to secure one of these roles is not acting for the department. Readers tracking other federal hiring may want <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/opm-federal-hiring-fair-29-october-20261028">the federal hiring fair roundup</a>, <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/cbp-november-recruiting-events-20261030">Customs and Border Protection November recruiting events</a>, and <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/us-job-cuts-october-2026-ai-153074-20261103">the October 2026 United States job cuts report</a>, which puts the wider hiring picture in context.</p>
<p><small>Sources: the official USAJOBS announcement at https://www.usajobs.gov/job/889245400, the NAN Jobs Portal summary at https://nan-usamilitaryjobs.surge.sh/articles/va-veterans-service-representative-hiring-october-2026.html, and the VA hiring announcement as reported at https://www.linkedin.com/posts/armandcuret_careeropportunities-federaljobs-veteransaffairs-activity-7523803929214742528-u5EX. The announcement states the grades, pay band, cutoffs, closing date and eligibility quoted here; the figure of more than 2,000 hires is the department's stated plan for fiscal year 2027.</small></p>$$,
'',
ARRAY['https://www.usajobs.gov/job/889245400','https://nan-usamilitaryjobs.surge.sh/articles/va-veterans-service-representative-hiring-october-2026.html','https://www.linkedin.com/posts/armandcuret_careeropportunities-federaljobs-veteransaffairs-activity-7523803929214742528-u5EX'],
NOW(), NOW(), NOW())
ON CONFLICT ("slug") DO NOTHING;


INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt") VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'xai-ai-tutor-jobs-remote-20261105', 'global', 'USA',
'xAI AI Tutor Jobs: 5 Remote Roles at $60–$90 an Hour, Apply on the Greenhouse Board',
'',
'xAI has five AI Tutor roles open for remote work in the United States, the United Kingdom, Canada and Australia, paying a typical $60 to $90 an hour.',
'',
$$<p>xAI AI Tutor jobs are open again, with five remote roles listed on 5 November 2026 for people who want to train Grok, the chatbot built by xAI, the company now known as SpaceXAI. The open roles pay a typical $60 to $90 an hour, with a median advertised rate of $60 an hour, and cover domain experts, mathematics and science specialists, and AI evaluation work. The roles are remote and full-time or part-time, but every one is a six-month temporary post, and the work is hired directly by the lab rather than through a data-labelling marketplace.</p>
<p>Read the limits first. The tutor postings name only the United States, the United Kingdom, Canada and Australia, with India accepted for two science roles, and xAI said it does not sponsor visas and cannot hire in Wyoming or Illinois. Pay is published only for United States-based candidates, and pay for applicants elsewhere is shared only during recruitment. The roles are six-month temporary positions that can change with minimal notice, and xAI has cut and paused this programme before, so applicants should treat the work as fixed-term hourly work rather than a permanent job.</p>
<table><tr><th>At a glance</th><th>Details</th></tr><tr><td>Company</td><td>xAI, now SpaceXAI (job board headed SpaceXSI), maker of Grok</td></tr><tr><td>Roles open</td><td>5 AI Tutor roles, verified on 5 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Typical pay</td><td>$60 to $90 an hour; median advertised rate $60 an hour</td></tr><tr><td>Pay range in postings</td><td>$35 to $100 an hour, depending on the role</td></tr><tr><td>Duration</td><td>6 months, temporary; full-time or part-time</td></tr><tr><td>Work mode</td><td>Remote</td></tr><tr><td>Countries named</td><td>United States, United Kingdom, Canada and Australia; India for two science roles</td></tr><tr><td>Visa sponsorship</td><td>Not provided; cannot hire in Wyoming or Illinois</td></tr><tr><td>Closing date</td><td>Not stated in the postings</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>xAI Greenhouse job board at job-boards.greenhouse.io/xai</td></tr></table>
<h2>xAI AI Tutor jobs: the five open roles</h2>
<p>The five open roles split across three kinds of work. Two are Domain Expert roles paying a typical $45 to $100 an hour with the highest rate at $100 an hour, two are Mathematics and Science roles paying a typical $45 to $75 an hour, and one is an AI Evaluation role paying a typical $40 to $75 an hour. Across the five roles, all of them stated an hourly rate, and the work covers language tutoring plus science, technology, engineering and mathematics, legal, design, humanities, writing and video specialists.</p>
<p>Tutors annotate, evaluate and write the data the model learns from. Language tutors need the language at CEFR C1 level or above and English at B2 or above, with native proficiency preferred, and experience in transcription, translation, localisation, voice recording or linguistics helps. Writing tutors need native or CEFR C2 English and verifiable proof of qualification in at least one specialty, with most specialties asking for five or more years of professional work and a public portfolio. Science and mathematics tutors need a master's degree or doctorate in the field and English at C1 or above, or a medal in the International Mathematical Olympiad or a comparable competition. Legal and compliance tutors need a law degree, active bar admission in good standing and at least two years of practising law.</p>
<h2>Who can apply for the xAI AI Tutor roles</h2>
<p>Applicants need the right to work from their country without sponsorship, and the posting must name their country. The roles suit native speakers of the posted languages, published writers, lawyers, mathematics and science postgraduates, designers and video editors in the United States, the United Kingdom, Canada or Australia who want six months of hourly work from a frontier lab. They do not suit anyone outside those countries, anyone needing visa sponsorship, anyone living in Wyoming or Illinois, or anyone needing work past six months.</p>
<p>Eligible United States staff get health insurance, a 401(k) plan and paid sick leave, according to the postings. Applicants apply with a resume and the evidence the role asks for, such as language levels, a portfolio, degrees or writing samples, and then report a CodeSignal assessment and a short video interview, followed by a conditional offer, a background check and onboarding. The hiring data shows the programme is volatile: open roles fell from 27 to 5 between 8 October 2026 and 4 November 2026, and xAI listed 15 new roles and removed 37 in that period.</p>
<h2>The record to weigh before applying for xAI AI Tutor jobs</h2>
<p>Applicants should weigh the programme's recent history. In September 2025 xAI told about 500 data annotation workers, a third of a 1,500-person team, that it no longer needed most generalist AI tutors, paying them to 30 November 2025 or their contract end but removing system access at once, and the company said it would grow its specialist tutor team instead. Bloomberg reported in June 2026 that xAI had paused hiring specialists to train Grok, with the pause described as temporary and partly caused by recruitment volumes. Some tutors have also complained about monitoring software on personal laptops and about the difficulty of skipping explicit or disturbing material in practice.</p>
<p>None of that makes the current postings illegitimate: xAI hires its tutors itself and prints the hourly band on every posting for United States candidates, from $35 an hour for language roles to $100 an hour for legal and compliance work. But the combination of six-month contracts, a history of sudden cuts and a fast-changing headcount means applicants should read the posting for the exact role, confirm the country and pay terms in writing, and keep other options open.</p>
<h2>How to apply for xAI AI Tutor jobs</h2>
<p>Go to xAI's own Greenhouse job board at job-boards.greenhouse.io/xai, now headed SpaceXSI, and pick the AI Tutor posting that matches your subject. Apply with your resume and the evidence the role asks for, then expect a CodeSignal assessment and a short video interview. Real openings are only on that board, so be wary of anyone who contacts you first on chat about an xAI role: the United States Federal Trade Commission said never to pay to get a job and to ignore unexpected job texts and messages on WhatsApp or Telegram.</p>
<p>Apply only through the official board and never pay an agent or recruiter for access to these roles. Readers weighing other AI training work may want <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/ai-training-jobs-software-engineers-20261104">AI training jobs for software engineers</a>, <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/ai-training-jobs-consultants-20261104">AI training jobs for consultants</a>, and <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/robot-training-jobs-1136-roles-20261104">robot training jobs</a>, which list 1,136 open roles in the same kind of work.</p>
<p><small>Sources: AITraining.jobs at https://aitraining.jobs/platforms/xai, which checks the xAI job board hourly and verified five open roles on 5 November 2026, and the xAI Greenhouse job board at https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/xai. The pay figures, country limits and six-month terms are taken from the postings as read on 29 October 2026 and 5 November 2026; the September 2025 cuts were reported by TechCrunch and the June 2026 hiring pause by Bloomberg.</small></p>$$,
'',
ARRAY['https://aitraining.jobs/platforms/xai','https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/xai'],
NOW(), NOW(), NOW())
ON CONFLICT ("slug") DO NOTHING;

